1
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:06,080
Okay, this is it.

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,380
You sure you wanna do this?

3
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:14,840
Hello, Mrs. Ross. Woo-hoo!

4
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:18,260
Well, hello, Mr. Rachel.

5
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,270
- Whoa!     - Oh, my God.

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,230
Come on, Pheebs, hurry! Hurry, hurry, hurry.

7
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,150
Okay! Okay!

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,990
Oh, my God! Is everybody getting married?

9
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:42,750
- Agh.     - No running in the chapel.

10
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,910
Hey, don't you give me any of your... Hey!

11
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:47,580
- Hi.     - Hey!

12
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,000
What are you doing here?

13
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:52,420
Ross and Rachel left a message. They're getting married.

14
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:54,510
- Isn't that why you guys are here?     - Yes.

15
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:56,840
- Why else would we be here?     - Ha-ha-ha.

16
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,760
Well, what happened? Did we miss it?

17
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:03,310
We actually missed it.

18
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,640
Maybe you wouldn't have if you could run in the chapel!

19
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:08,980
This is insane.

20
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:12,150
What's the big deal? It's not like it's a real marriage.

21
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,150
What?

22
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,160
If you marry in Vegas, you're only married in Vegas.

23
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:23,240
What? If you marry here, you're married everywhere.

24
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:24,580
Really?

25
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,250
Yeah.

26
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,960
Oh, my God.

27
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:31,880
Oh, well.

28
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000

29
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,260
Mm.

30
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:50,120
Why are we in bed together?

31
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:51,620
I don't know.

32
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,840
Do you have any clothes on?

33
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:57,710
Yes.

34
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,170
- Really?     - No.

35
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,800
Ugh...

36
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:05,220
But we didn't have...

37
00:03:06,510 --> 00:03:08,770
sex, did we?

38
00:03:10,770 --> 00:03:13,310
I don't remember much about last night.

39
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,730
- It was such a blur. Ha, ha.     - Oh.

40
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,110
Oh!

41
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:21,280
- I remember laughing. I laughed a lot.     - Uh-huh?

42
00:03:21,450 --> 00:03:22,860
Then we didn't have sex.

43
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:31,160
Oh, I mean, we were really drunk.

44
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:33,170
I'm glad we didn't do anything stupid.

45
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:35,000
Tell me about it.

46
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:42,170
- Morning, Pheebs.     - Mm.

47
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:45,930
Well, my movie has been officially canceled.

48
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,760
Mm. Joey, I'm so sorry.

49
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:50,180
You want my breakfast?

50
00:03:50,350 --> 00:03:52,890
Eh, too depressed to eat.

51
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,440
I'll probably eat in, like, five minutes.

52
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:59,400
So I guess I'll fly home with you. What time is your flight?

53
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:02,190
- What about my cab?     - I don't need that anymore.

54
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:06,030
No, you borrowed my cab. You have to drive it back.

55
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:09,280
I don't wanna drive back by myself. I get lonely.

56
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:12,040
Oh, ooh. How about if you come with me?

57
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,540
- I don't know, it's a long trip.     - That would be great.

58
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:17,170
We could talk and play games.

59
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:21,380
This could be our chance to, like, renew our friendship.

60
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:25,090
Are you asking me to have a "frienaissance"?

61
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:27,970
Sure?

62
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:33,270
Heh. All right, although I don't think we need one. I never stopped loving you.

63
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,060
- Hey.     - Hey.

64
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:37,270
- Hey.     - Hey.

65
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:40,020
So has anybody talked to Dr. And Mrs. Geller yet?

66
00:04:40,190 --> 00:04:43,240
Mm-hm. They left me a message. They'll be here.

67
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:45,700
Where is the waitress? I'm starving.

68
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:49,870
It's a buffet, man.

69
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:53,540
Here's where I win all my money back!

70
00:04:56,210 --> 00:04:57,460
I gotta talk to you.

71
00:04:57,670 --> 00:04:58,710
Sure.

72
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,090
What's up?

73
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,850
Monica and I almost got married.

74
00:05:11,010 --> 00:05:12,470
My God!

75
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,310
That's huge! Ha-ha-ha, hey.

76
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,900
Wait a minute. Why wasn't I invited?

77
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:24,110
And who was gonna be your best man? Don't say Ross. Do not say Ross.

78
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:28,660
I just don't think that Monica and I are ready yet. I love her...

79
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:32,370
but seeing Ross and Rachel come out of that chapel...

80
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:37,580
was like a wake-up call that Monica and I are moving so fast, you know.

81
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:40,880
How do I tell her without crushing her?

82
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,540
Oh!

83
00:05:43,210 --> 00:05:45,510
Tell her she's not marriage material.

84
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,840
What?

85
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,470
Girls say it to me all the time.

86
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:58,440
And if she's anything like me, she's just gonna be relieved.

87
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:02,610
How do I tell him that it's too soon?

88
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,230
He's gonna think I don't love him anymore.

89
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,740
- Well, you don't.     - Yes, I do.

90
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,860
Good. I was just testing you.

91
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:13,240
- Hey.     - Oh, hi.

92
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:15,580
We were just talking about bacon.

93
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:18,040
No, we were talking about tennis.

94
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:20,500
Tennis is more believable.

95
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,090
Hey.

96
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:27,300
- Hi.     - Thank you.

97
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:31,390
- Coffee. Heh.     - Mm.

98
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,480
- What?     - Are we gonna talk...

99
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,850
about what you guys did last night, or?

100
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:48,490
What do you mean "last night"? Nothing, uh, happened last night.

101
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:51,990
Uh-huh. Ross invited us all to watch.

102
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:57,240
Rach, we weren't gonna miss our friends marrying.

103
00:06:57,410 --> 00:06:59,330
Huh, who got married?

104
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,920
You did?

105
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:05,170
- What?     - Heh.

106
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:08,920
- Wh...? Hello. We didn't get married.     - No, we didn't. That's ridi...

107
00:07:14,550 --> 00:07:17,470
Wait, wait, wait. I remember being in a chapel.

108
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:21,140
They would not let us get married when we were that drunk.

109
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:23,400
They let you get married.

110
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,810
Most people who marry in Vegas are drunk.

111
00:07:27,230 --> 00:07:29,150
Heh, I'm drunk right now.

112
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:34,780
I can't have a mimosa with breakfast? I'm on vacation.

113
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,620
What are you gonna do?

114
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:39,240
- Well, I guess we find a divorce lawyer.     - Uh-huh.

115
00:07:39,450 --> 00:07:42,580
Well, I think, I think Ross already has one.

116
00:07:45,330 --> 00:07:46,790
Now, this one's free, right?

117
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,380
Because you paid for the first two, third one free.

118
00:07:50,050 --> 00:07:52,300
Laugh it up, but the joke's on you...

119
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:55,010
because we don't need to get divorced.

120
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:58,050
- We're just gonna get an annulment.     - An annulment?

121
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:01,730
Ross, I don't think surgery is the answer here.

122
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,850
Oh, that's your thing!

123
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:07,940
What?

124
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:12,150
Your thing, that you're the guy who gets divorced.

125
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:13,820
Oh, yeah.

126
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:16,450
No, no, that's not "my thing."

127
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:19,160
I do not love getting divorced.

128
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,750
Yes, you do. This is your third divorce.

129
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:26,580
You love divorce so much, you're probably gonna marry it...

130
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:31,800
and then it won't work out, so you're gonna have to divorce it, divorcing guy.

131
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,590
Ha-ha-ha.

132
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:35,470
I'm so drunk.

133
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:45,520
- So, what should we do?     - I don't know.

134
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:47,400
I know I love you.

135
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,520
- I know I love you.     - Heh.

136
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,660
Where are we on the whole "going back...

137
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:59,870
to where they have the marriages" thing? I love you.

138
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,370
That's a good question.

139
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,410
Last night we let the dice decide.

140
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:08,580
We should leave it up to fate again. I love you!

141
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,380
We don't get married unless there's a sign.

142
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,170
Okay? So say, uh...

143
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:17,430
You roll another eight, then there's a sign that we should get married.

144
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:19,220
All right. Eight we get married...

145
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:23,770
but 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, we don't get married.

146
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,100
- Sounds great.     - Okay.

147
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:27,140
Hey, we got a shooter.

148
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,690
Money, please.

149
00:09:28,850 --> 00:09:29,940
- Ready?     - Ready.

150
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:31,980
Come on, eight.

151
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,070
Yes, yes, eight.

152
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,950
Eight, easy eight.

153
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:47,620
- Wow, I can't believe I rolled an eight.     - That was so unlikely.

154
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:52,840
- Well, let's get married. I guess.     - Aah.

155
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,510
That wasn't hard. Last night I rolled a hard eight.

156
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:58,630
It was the wrong kind of eight. No wedding! Damn it!

157
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:02,100
- Agh! Aah!     - Unh, I wanted it so bad!

158
00:10:04,930 --> 00:10:05,970
- Wanna go pack?     - Yeah.

159
00:10:09,230 --> 00:10:12,060
- We're doing the right thing, right?     - Oh, of course we are.

160
00:10:12,230 --> 00:10:14,440
Heh, we left it up to fate.

161
00:10:14,610 --> 00:10:18,280
If we were supposed to get married, there would be a sign.

162
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:30,170
Okay, you have 19 questions left. Use them wisely.

163
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:36,050
Come on, Joey. You can't win if you don't ask any...

164
00:10:36,210 --> 00:10:37,260
questions!

165
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:39,470
Aah! Aah.

166
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:43,050
- What?     - You promised me a fun road trip.

167
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:46,930
We've been on the road for 6 hours, and you've been asleep for 5 and a half.

168
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:50,390
We are switching, and you are going to drive back.

169
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:54,440
That will be your punishment, you greedy sleeper.

170
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,480
All right. All right.

171
00:10:56,690 --> 00:10:59,570
Yeah. And until then, you are going to sing to me.

172
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:04,120
Because the radio's broken, and you are selfish, but you have a nice voice.

173
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,620
- Really?     - Sing!

174
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:12,460
# I wanna rock 'n' roll all night #

175
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:21,720
Man, this is a long drive.

176
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:24,590
Are my eyes open?

177
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,300
No!

178
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,700
- Morning.     - Aah!

179
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:52,410
- Hey.     - Hey, hubby. Heh.

180
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,960
Yeah. Actually, um, I wanted to talk to you...

181
00:11:58,130 --> 00:12:00,550
- about that whole annulment thing.     - Uh-huh?

182
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,800
Yeah, I'm not gonna do that.

183
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:17,610
- Okay.     - Heh.

184
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:21,150
So we'll just stay married.

185
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,650
Yes, exactly.

186
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:26,660
And I will make everyone call me Mrs. Geller.

187
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,950
Wow, this is so amazing.

188
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:34,000
I, uh, really thought I'd have to talk you into this more.

189
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:39,000
Ha, ha. Now I'm scared because I don't actually think you're kidding.

190
00:12:40,380 --> 00:12:42,090
I'm not kidding.

191
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:43,800
Look, I... I... Heh.

192
00:12:43,970 --> 00:12:47,220
I can't have three failed marriages.

193
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,050
I can't, okay?

194
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:52,430
I am not gonna be that guy.

195
00:12:56,230 --> 00:12:58,730
So, what, we just stay married forever?

196
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:00,440
Okay, how...?

197
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:03,570
How is this going to affect you, really?

198
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:09,530
I mean, you fill some form out once in a while...

199
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:13,910
instead of checking the box "Miss," you check the box that says, "Mrs."

200
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:17,040
It's right next to it.

201
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:21,840
Okay. I'm sorry, you're right. You know what?

202
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:23,800
We can stay married...

203
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:28,640
because I thought that the boxes were far away from each other.

204
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:33,350
All right. Look, just...

205
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,520
please take a moment here...

206
00:13:35,730 --> 00:13:38,650
and think about what you're asking of me. Okay?

207
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:44,070
I am asking you to do me a favor.

208
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:49,910
You are asking me to be your wife.

209
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:55,040
And, as my wife, I think you should grant me this favor.

210
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:01,080
That kid kicked me really hard.

211
00:14:01,290 --> 00:14:03,290
Well, you did pull his hair.

212
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:06,840
- He took my snack.     - I'm not getting into this again.

213
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:09,630
All right, you know what? Hurts really bad.

214
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,890
Well, I told you not to walk. Here.

215
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:13,560
There. There. Okay.

216
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:25,650
- This doesn't mean anything, does it?     - No.

217
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:31,660
How could you pick up a hitchhiker?

218
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:36,490
He could be a rape... He could be a rapist or a killer or something.

219
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:39,410
Don't you think I asked him that before he got in?

220
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,920
I'm not talking to you. You go back to sleep.

221
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:45,590
- And, you, are you a rapist?     - No.

222
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:47,510
Do you like car games?

223
00:14:47,670 --> 00:14:49,970
Yeah, you know the, uh, license plate game?

224
00:14:50,130 --> 00:14:51,890
I love the license plate game!

225
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:54,010
Ooh, I'll play. I'll play.

226
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:56,260
No, you need your sleep. Night-night. Shh.

227
00:15:03,150 --> 00:15:04,230
- Hey.     - Hey.

228
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,860
Listen. I know you wanted to talk to me...

229
00:15:07,030 --> 00:15:10,530
but I have an idea that may make you wanna stay married.

230
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:12,200
Uh...

231
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,240
We register...

232
00:15:14,410 --> 00:15:17,040
and you get to keep all the presents.

233
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:23,880
No, Ross, come on. No, listen.

234
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:28,130
I've thought about how to tell you this, and, um, the bottom line, Ross...

235
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,920
is we cannot stay married.

236
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,800
- I don't know if that's true...     - Oh, but it is.

237
00:15:35,970 --> 00:15:38,430
Ahem. Okay. You know what this is?

238
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:42,350
This is a difference of opinion.

239
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,020
- When that happens in a marriage...     - Oh, Ross, come on!

240
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:51,190
This is not a marriage! This is the world's worst hangover!

241
00:15:52,570 --> 00:15:55,660
Ross, listen, if you do not get this annulment, I will.

242
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,540
All right. All right, I'll do it.

243
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,120
Thank you.

244
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:06,330
Hey, hey, um...

245
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:10,090
uh, is there any such thing as an annulment shower?

246
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:16,760
There's the train station, where I get off.

247
00:16:16,930 --> 00:16:19,260
Well, I have your address and phone number.

248
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:22,560
And I have your name and the fact that you're a drifter.

249
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:25,560
So ball's pretty much in your court.

250
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,150
All right. See you, Pheebs.

251
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:39,410
Come on, Pheebs, I can't take this anymore.

252
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:40,870
Please talk to me.

253
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:45,710
Let me make it up to you, huh?

254
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:50,710
# Ground control to Major Tom #

255
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:55,970
# Commencing countdown Engines on #

256
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:04,350
# Take your protein pills And put your helmet on #

257
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,270
# Pssh, this is... #

258
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,900
Stop it! Stop it! No.

259
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:13,860
That's not fair. You know I can't resist that beautiful voice.

260
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:17,320
Pheebs, look, I am so sorry.

261
00:17:17,490 --> 00:17:20,200
I promised you a fun road trip with your friend...

262
00:17:20,450 --> 00:17:23,120
and I didn't deliver, okay?

263
00:17:23,330 --> 00:17:28,290
Now I know that you think being awake is an important part of friendship.

264
00:17:29,330 --> 00:17:33,340
So I will strive to stay awake for as long as I know you.

265
00:17:36,050 --> 00:17:38,550
You can still sleep at night and stuff.

266
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,050
Thank you.

267
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,100
So can we play 20 Questions now?

268
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:47,140
I got a good one. I thought about it since Kansas.

269
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:50,150
Okay.

270
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:52,440
Is it...

271
00:17:52,650 --> 00:17:55,030
a kind of hot sandwich?

272
00:17:55,690 --> 00:17:57,070
Yes.

273
00:17:58,110 --> 00:17:59,740
Is it a meatball sub?

274
00:17:59,990 --> 00:18:01,910
That is incredible!

275
00:18:02,410 --> 00:18:04,290
You are the master!

276
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,370
Aah! Bug!

277
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:14,420
- Ah! That's funny. You look like you're...     - Don't say it!

278
00:18:14,590 --> 00:18:16,300
Don't even think it.

279
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,800
All right.

280
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:20,640
Chandler, enjoy your handful.

281
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,720
Should we just get married?

282
00:18:26,930 --> 00:18:29,890
All the signs are telling us to do it.

283
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:31,270
I'm sick of the signs.

284
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:34,070
- I'm happy the way things are.     - Me too.

285
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,070
- I don't want change, do you?     - No.

286
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:39,530
All right then, nothing changes. Everything stays the same!

287
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:43,490
Go unpack. It's been three days, and it's driving me insane!

288
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:47,910
Jeez, relax, it's not like we're mar... Aah, agh.

289
00:18:57,550 --> 00:18:59,760
You know, I was thinking, what if I, uh...

290
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:01,800
unpack here?

291
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:03,720
All your stuff would be here.

292
00:19:05,930 --> 00:19:07,180
Well...

293
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,810
What if all my stuff was here?

294
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:15,310
Then you'd be going back and forth all the time.

295
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,650
Doesn't make any sense.

296
00:19:18,030 --> 00:19:19,490
Okay.

297
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:25,200
What if we live together, and you understand what I'm saying?

298
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,120
Live together?

299
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,620
There've been no signs for that.

300
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:35,960
Me asking is kind of a sign.

301
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:42,430
- Yes! Yes! Yes!     - Okay!

302
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:47,850
Yes.

303
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,220
Okay. Okay, wait. Wait, wait, wait.

304
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:52,480
- Okay.     - Here's your key. Here's your key.

305
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:54,310
Now go out and christen it!

306
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:55,940
Go out and come back in!

307
00:19:56,150 --> 00:19:58,690
Door hasn't been locked in five years, but okay.

308
00:20:00,190 --> 00:20:01,780
- Ready?     - Ready!

309
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:05,990
The key broke in the lock, and I can't get in.

310
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,910
Wait. Oh, my God, I can't get out!

311
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:11,790
- This isn't a sign!     - No, it's a very old key!

312
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,330
- It's an old key!     - Oh, my God, it's old.

313
00:20:15,210 --> 00:20:16,420
I love you.

314
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,960
I love you.

315
00:20:20,630 --> 00:20:23,720
Are you hugging the door right now?

316
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:30,390
No.

317
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:33,520
Yeah, yeah, me neither.

318
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,400
Hey.

319
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:40,730
So did everything go all right with the annulment?

320
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:43,860
Oh, yeah. No problems. It's all taken care of.

321
00:20:44,070 --> 00:20:45,360
Ross, thank you.

322
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,620
Do you wanna go see a movie?

323
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:50,620
- Yeah, why not?     - Pheebs?

324
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:52,700
Thanks, I've already seen one.

325
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:57,120
- Okay, um, I'm gonna get my sweater.     - Okay.

326
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:02,380
You wanna hear something weird?

327
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,970
Always.

328
00:21:05,590 --> 00:21:07,720
I didn't get the annulment.

329
00:21:09,550 --> 00:21:12,100
- What?     - We're still married.

330
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,560
Don't tell Rachel. See you later.

331
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:23,180

332
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:30,740
What are you doing?

333
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:32,450
Key is stuck in the lock.

334
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:34,200
I can fix it. Hold on.

335
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:37,750
Watch out, watch out.

336
00:21:44,050 --> 00:21:45,260
It still doesn't work.

337
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:46,920
- I'm not finished.     - Oh.

338
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:01,020
Nice job, Joe. You are quite the craftsman.

